    "explanation": "Let CP1=30, CP2=40. Total CP=70. Total SP=70*1.2=84. SP1+SP2=84. Ratio 5:6 => SP1=84*(5/11)=420/11~38.18. Profit1 = (38.18-30)/30 = 27.2%. Let's make ratio exact: CP1=3x, CP2=4x. SP1=5y, SP2=6y. 5y+6y = 1.2(7x) => 11y = 8.4x => y = 8.4/11 x. SP1 = 5 * 8.4/11 x = 42/11 x. Profit1 = (42/11 x - 3x)/3x = (42/11 - 33/11)/3 = (9/11)/3 = 3/11 = 27.2%. Let's change ratios. CP1:CP2=1:2, SP1:SP2=1:1. Total profit 20%. CP=3, SP=3.6. SP1=1.8. CP1=1. Profit=80%. Let's use: CP1:CP2=2:3, SP1:SP2=4:5. Total CP=5x. SP=6x (20% profit). 4y+5y=6x => 9y=6x => y=2/3 x. SP1=8/3 x. CP1=2x. Profit = (8/3 - 2)/2 = 2/3 / 2 = 1/3 = 33.33%."
